# runtime/ holds run/audit scripts (keep in version control) plus generated
# outputs (ignore). The previous `runtime/` + `!runtime/*.py` pair tracked
# NOTHING: git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory, so every
# run script and every acceptance-audit script was unversioned. Un-exclude the
# directories first, then the script files.
runtime/**
!runtime/**/
!runtime/**/*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
# `.env` alone does not match `.env.local` / `.env.production`; without these
# two lines a single `git add -A` writes credentials into the history that is
# meant to be handed to other people.
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
# Build artifacts from `python -m build` / pip wheel; never hand these out.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
